  "notes": "Substitutions from the four-engine granite-4.1-3b run, each engine-level and disclosed: (1) MODEL - granite-4.1-3b (GraniteForCausalLM) is not in TRT-LLM 1.2.1's model registry ('Unknown architecture for AutoModelForCausalLM: GraniteForCausalLM'), so Qwen3-1.7B (Qwen3ForCausalLM, a TRT-LLM-supported arch with a matching --tool_parser qwen3) was served instead; the truncation property is an engine guarantee, not model quality, so this measures TRT-LLM's behaviour, not a quality cross-compare. (2) tool_choice - TRT-LLM 1.2.1's OpenAI server rejects tool_choice:\"required\" with HTTP 400 (accepts only none/auto/named); \"auto\" is used, which with this prompt+tools forces the call at every budget (the model emits the tool call from the first token). A named tool_choice DOES force but bypasses the qwen3 parser and dumps the raw <tool_call> framing into arguments unparseably at every rung including the control, so it is not a valid truncation measurement. (3) enable_thinking=false - Qwen3 is a reasoning model; with thinking on it spends the whole budget in <think> and never reaches the JSON even at 64 (control fails), so thinking is disabled to make it a direct tool-caller comparable to granite.",
